            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Organisms rely on nociceptive sensory neurons to detect and avoid potentially tissue-damaging stimuli in the environment. New research has unraveled previously unknown downstream neural circuit components for nociceptive (pain-like) behavior in Drosophila larvae.</AbstractText>
